summary explains, it does not grant.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this
software and its associated files, to:

  (a) use it for any purpose that is not commercial, including on private and
      public servers, in videos, streams and other published recordings;

  (b) redistribute the software unmodified and in full, free of charge, provided
      that this license and the credits are included unchanged and that the
      origin is stated;

  (c) include it in a modpack or server pack that is distributed free of charge,
      under the same conditions as (b);

  (d) modify it for your own private use, and for the purpose of preparing
      contributions to be offered back to this project;

  (e) copy parts of the source code into a mod of your own, including a mod you
      sell, provided that:

        (i)   your mod is its own work. This code may be an ingredient in it,
              not its substance. A mod whose point is what NPC Studio does, and
              which carries NPC Studio's code in order to do it, is a
              republication under section 2(b) however much was rewritten;

        (ii)  NPC Studio and its author are named where a person will find
              them — your credits, your project page, or a header in the copied
              file. This is a condition and not a courtesy: without it, the
              permission in (e) does not apply;

        (iii) you do not present the copied code as your own work.

      This permission covers source code and the data formats defined in it. It
      does not cover textures, models, icons, sounds or animations, and it never
      covers third-party content (section 5);

  (f) write add-ons, integrations and ports against this mod's API, and
      distribute them on whatever terms you choose, including paid ones. A mod
      that depends on NPC Studio without carrying its code is not restricted by
      section 2.

Ideas are outside this license, and could not be placed inside it: copyright
covers this particular code and these particular assets, not the notions behind
them. Branching dialogue, an editor for it inside the game, a wardrobe of
skins — take the idea and build your own. No permission is given because none
is required. Saying where an idea came from costs nothing and is appreciated;
unlike (e)(ii), that one is a courtesy and not a condition.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

  (a) Sell it, charge for access to it, or make it part of any paid product,
      paid service, paid rank, paid modpack or paywalled download. Accepting
      donations that are not required for access is not selling. Code borrowed
      under 1(e) is the exception: it may travel into a paid mod, because what
      is sold there is that mod and not this one.

  (b) Publish it, or any modified version of it, as a separate project of your
      own — on Modrinth, CurseForge, GitHub or anywhere else. Sharing a private
      modification with the people you play with is not publishing, and neither
      is a mod of your own that borrows code under 1(e).

  (c) Remove, obscure or alter the authorship, the credits, or this license, or
      present the work as your own.

  (d) Train a machine-learning model on this source with the purpose of
      reproducing it.


3. ASKING

Anything not granted above may still be granted. Ask, and the answer may well be
yes — a port to a Minecraft version this project has not reached, or a fork
continued if this project goes quiet, are exactly the sort of thing worth
asking about. Silence is not permission, but a question costs nothing.


4. CONTRIBUTIONS

By offering a contribution to this project, you agree that it may be distributed
under this license. You keep the copyright to what you wrote.


5. THIRD-PARTY CONTENT

This license covers the code and assets authored by this project. Some content
distributed alongside it was made by other people and carries its own terms;
those parts are named, with their authors, in the credits. Nothing here grants
you rights over somebody else's work.


6. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS
FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR
COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER
IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN
